WEBVTT

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.440
It's impossible to resist causality.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.270
This is the correction of chaos.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:15.110
It seems that you weren't
meant to be there after all.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.740
You will be sent back to the start.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.580
What are you saying?

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:26.080
You will experience the 
same events over again.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.920
But don't forget that
they'll be slightly different.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.670
Takuya, remember this.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.850
Causality rules everything in this world.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.930
To discover its secrets 
is to explore history.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.100
What does that mean?

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.820
Hey, answer me!

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.150
Dad! Dad!

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.330
Mt. Sankaku?

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.000
I'm restarting from here?

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.500
It's gonna be awful
if I've got to keep doing this.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:49.020
"Episode 7: The Cause of the Curse"

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.480
Hello?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.730
This is your wake-up call!

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.610
Your superhero in your hour of need,
Masakatsu Yuki, is here!

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.910
How do you have that
kind of energy this early?

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.330
You seem like you're starting
your morning off on the wrong foot.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:08.000
It's summer break tomorrow! Summer break!

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.200
Summer break? Tomorrow?

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.820
Could you not sleep, boss?

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.500
I bet you slept too much in class.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:19.470
Actually, I saw a monster
that stalks the earth each night.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.760
The one from the curse?

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.720
Sometimes I think, you know,

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.770
that old legends and folk tales are real.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.680
What's got you so excited?

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.440
Somewhere there might be an entrance
that takes you to a world of mystery,

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.070
that only opens once
every a few hundred years!

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:36.900
Hold it.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.530
Who are you getting this from?

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.570
You can tell?

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.070
It was in a book by
Dr. Kodai Somebody-or-Other,

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.280
and it's fascinating!

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:45.450
Boss?

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.040
Hey, boss!

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:00.840
You will experience the 
same events over again.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.740
But don't forget that
they'll be slightly different.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.850
So it seems.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.230
Oh, Sensei, you're so silly!

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.900
Oh, Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:22.320
Oh? Didn't you two see
each just other last night?

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.460
I had something to do and couldn't make it.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.400
I was reduced to waiting in my home.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:32.160
Lately I'm staying indoors at night.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:34.750
I'm scared of the curse, you see.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.110
Oh, Sensei, you're so silly!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.710
I don't want to be the third victim.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.930
The teacher's not here.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.620
Th-This is...

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.490
Excuse me!

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.380
You've finally revealed your true nature!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.550
True nature?

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.550
You've gone from ordinary
pervert to mega-pervert!

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:25.970
Calm down, Mio.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:29.850
I'm the most straight-laced,
buttoned-down man in the world.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:34.240
Don't tell me that when
you're holding a pair of panties!

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:37.100
Anywhere, where's Eriko-<i>sensei</i>?

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.520
Don't ask me.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.890
So why are her clothes on the bed?

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:42.270
I don't know.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.780
Maybe she shed her cocoon and flew off?

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.570
She's not a butterfly!

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:48.490
And put her panties down!

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.030
Or here, give them to me.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.060
Bye!

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:55.430
Arima-<i>kun</i>!

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.250
Takuya.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:02.550
We need to talk.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:10.210
Don't you think something's
changed with Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>, lately?

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:11.990
Changed how?

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:17.310
Well, for example,
he used to criticize smoking.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.680
But now he's started getting into cigars.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.730
People go from non-smokers
to smokers all the time.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.320
First, his mom came to me.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.490
"Please marry my son?"

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.320
Don't joke about this.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:33.240
Sorry.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:37.580
She said he'd changed.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:39.680
And then I started to notice too.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.140
He was different.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:46.650
There's been something
bugging me about Ryuzoji, too.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.680
Have you seen him talking
with some odd people lately?

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.720
I have.

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:57.520
I know about a self-proclaimed
journalist named Kaori Asakura, and...

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.230
There's another.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.670
He's hired a detective.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.350
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.280
You okay?

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.110
Yeah.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.450
Just a migraine.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.080
I talked to Ryuzoji this morning.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.660
And something felt off.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.620
You too?

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:22.580
When he talked about the curse.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:26.150
I don't want to be the third victim.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.230
Third?

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:29.630
That's right.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:32.800
The news has only reported on one victim.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.180
Yeah, that is strange.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.770
It didn't feel like he misspoke.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:42.000
I'm taking my dad's research
materials to Ryuzoji's house today.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.560
I'll check on him.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:45.800
Thanks.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:50.070
There wasn't anybody else I could talk
to about this, so it's a huge help.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.540
Tell me if you see anything that feels wrong.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.380
We're done!

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.420
Once you turn in your handout,
you can go home.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.920
Yes!

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:14.130
You're going to Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>'s house, boss?

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:14.930
Yeah.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:16.850
I'm taking my dad's stuff over there.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:18.640
You're so brave.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:21.390
Isn't that mansion kind of scary?

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:22.890
You think so?

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:23.940
I want to go too.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:28.770
He promised earlier
to let me see his tapestry.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:31.280
I'm going to take some stuff.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.610
And he's all I need to help carry it.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.700
I'm going too?!

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.950
But it's awkward for me to go alone.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:41.000
This would be a good time.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.960
Well, I don't mind you coming.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.910
Want to come too, Kanna-<i>chan</i>?

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.960
I'm going home.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.760
You're not curious
about Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>'s house?

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.860
It's the place everybody's
talking about because of the curse.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.220
Ryuzoji-<i>san</i> smells different.

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:02.100
He smells different than everyone else.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:18.570
Hatano-<i>san</i>'s kind of tough to talk to.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.410
She is a little strange.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:21.910
And hot.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.830
She seems to be avoiding people deliberately.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.290
She is hot, though.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.540
She is hot...

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.800
Boys are so weak to girls like her.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.970
This place sure is eerie...

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:53.440
Is there something I can do for you?

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.150
I brought the documents
I was asked to bring.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:57.740
My name is Arima.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:09:59.470
I'm sorry?

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:03.570
Um... I called earlier...

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.160
Is that right?

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.750
When you get old, you get so forgetful.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.210
Come inside.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.720
It's a little cold today, isn't it?

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.850
Hey, walk normally!

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:29.270
There might be some kind of wild cat here!

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.470
Or alien.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.280
Boss, over there!

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.570
What?

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:39.360
It's just an old rotting storehouse.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:45.620
The mansion was originally built
400 years ago, and then remodeled.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.660
It seems like it's in bad shape, though.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:50.540
It's strange...

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:54.430
As if that storehouse
has gone back in time...

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:00.010
Now, did you come to see my son?

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.800
Yes, that's right.

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:04.730
He's changed, you know.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:08.270
He's not my son anymore.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:12.860
Have you ever heard the saying,

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:18.340
"The swallows and sparrows know
not the thoughts of geese and swans."

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.900
Think well about what it might mean.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.290
What are you talking about, mother?

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:31.870
Forgive me!

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.920
I didn't mean any harm.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.700
Please... forgive me!

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.970
Welcome to the center of the curse.

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:51.600
Sorry for scaring you.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:55.730
My mother has Alzheimer's.
She doesn't recognize her son anymore.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:57.230
I see.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:01.350
You're not that much different
in age than Ayumi-<i>kun</i>,

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:04.110
so I'm sure it's not
something you worry about.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.280
Yes, I guess.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:10.700
This place is huge.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:14.630
Maybe it just looks that way
'cause there's no furniture...

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.630
I got rid of anything that
wasn't related to my research.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.670
Right now, I don't even have a bed.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.630
How do you sleep?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.090
On the floor.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:26.970
That sounds painful.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:30.810
A soft bed makes me feel like I'm floating.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.480
It's hard to relax.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.210
This is the tapestry.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.400
Wow.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.950
It's huge.

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:45.820
Is this from 400 years ago too?

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:46.950
Probably.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.950
It's been here for many, many years.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:53.820
But it might be something from overseas
that was brought here 400 years ago, right?

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.380
Maybe it's even older.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.460
You're just like your father.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:03.970
Kodai Arima said the same thing.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.560
These people are burning, right?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:12.050
It's like they're suffering from the heat.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.640
Is it symbolic of something?

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.980
Like there's a hidden meaning.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:18.310
I see!

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:21.730
It's like some weird church from Europe.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:24.240
Yeah, it does feel religious.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:29.580
So this light is God punishing
mankind, or something?

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:33.320
What sin did they commit, you think?

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:37.210
Thank you for those very 
interesting opinions.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.340
I'll take them into consideration.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:44.170
Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>, may I make
a sketch of this tapestry?

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.420
Certainly.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.300
You seem to like it.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.300
Yes. It's wonderful.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:54.180
Actually, I didn't like this tapestry.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:55.680
Yeah.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:58.940
Looking at it's enough to make you
lose your appetite for mortal fun.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:05.690
But after Kodai showed interest in it,
I changed my mind.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:06.790
My dad was interested in it?

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:11.700
I was well aware of
the strength of Kodai's intuition.

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.670
I'd like to talk in private with Takuya-<i>kun</i>.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:18.550
Is that all right?

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.130
Yes, I'll stay here and make my sketch.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.710
I'll be here too.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.130
Come to my room, then.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:40.410
I always wanted to have
a chance to talk to you like this.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.170
Me too.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:48.030
You remind me a lot of
the Kodai Arima I remember.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.170
I have a question.

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:51.820
Go ahead.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.980
What was my father researching with you?

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:02.340
I'm going to have to go back
a long way to explain that.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:07.710
Kodai and I were classmates in college.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:12.550
Even then, we shared a common goal:

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.100
to discover the hidden elements of history,

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.980
the things they didn't put in the textbooks.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:23.560
Much later, Kodai was banished
from respectable academic society.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:28.940
"The 400-Year Cycle Hypothesis"

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:28.940
But I was extremely impressed
by his 400-Year Cycle theory.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:34.950
I invited him to come 
research at my university.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:38.330
Kodai focused on Sakaimachi as a place

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:43.420
to research both 400-Year Cycle theory
and the Takanoamahara people.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.170
And then he met a physicist,
Yurika Imagawa, who was investigating the fact

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:51.050
that the magnetic and
gravitational fields of Sakaimachi

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:54.020
were different than other places.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.660
We engaged in heated debate.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:04.190
Professor Imagawa pursued a unified theory,
based on quantum mechanics.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:08.190
And I chose humans themselves
for my research theme.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:15.570
And your father, Kodai Arima,
chose immortality for his research theme.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.370
Immortality?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.290
Is that surprising?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:23.710
I didn't think he was that crazy...

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:30.510
By the way, what do you think
the dawn of the universe was like?

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:32.760
Or the dawn of this world, if you prefer.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.800
What's this about?

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.140
I'm curious as to your opinion.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:41.810
One scientist says that
the universe has always existed.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:44.190
That doesn't seem realistic to me.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.300
"Eternity" isn't real.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:49.650
Another theory is the big bang.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:53.240
Oh, the one that says a small
high-density nucleus exploded,

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:54.990
and became the universe.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.450
What do you think of that theory?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:01.330
Well, it's better than "eternity."

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:07.640
Then before the big bang, what existed
around the "small nucleus" you speak of?

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:11.290
I don't know.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:16.340
Our job as researchers is
to theorize about inexplicable events,

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:19.410
and then prove those theories.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.900
Let's return to the subject at hand.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:26.940
When we were working together,
Professor Imagawa's research notes

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:31.190
spoke of a woman who lived
in reclusion near Ken-no-Misaki.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:39.160
She was blind, with shining
gold hair and pure white skin.

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:43.080
Her name was Keitia, later changed to Keiko.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:46.220
She was your mother.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.250
The boss said it was symbolic...

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:54.260
If you look closely and listen carefully,

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:57.510
you should be able to discover a
message from people in the distant past.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:05.390
Through his research,
Kodai became close to Keiko-<i>san</i>.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:07.310
And then you were born.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:15.320
I barely remember my mother.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:19.620
It was hard to believe she was blind.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:21.580
She helped with Kodai's research.

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.700
And took care of you when you were sick.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:24.580
Sick?

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:29.240
You seemed to get fevers all
the time when you were young.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:39.250
I guess sending you after 
Kodai is one option...

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:48.850
Hey, this is an entrance, right?

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.680
Yeah, now that you mention it...

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:54.780
It reminds me of something.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.090
Of what?

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.040
We've gone off topic.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.620
Takuya Arima,

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.680
may I ask you a question?

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.700
If it's something I can tell you...

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:19.300
Did Kodai give you something?

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:22.050
No idea.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:24.560
He just up and died on me.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:30.140
Then did he leave you anything?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.560
What do you mean?

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.280
For example,

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.910
something similar to a time machine.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.130
Well?

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.160
No.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:48.720
This is weird...

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.410
I'm feeling dizzy...

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:57.290
I believe that Kodai found the
truth hidden here in Sakaimachi.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:19:59.010
What's wrong?

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.730
You're sweating.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.630
No, um...

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:04.600
What is this?

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.640
Ryuzoji's doing something...

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:11.290
You should have a device Kodai gave you.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:16.040
Now give me what you have!

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:20.920
Do it now!

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:27.380
He was able to resist the Niarb?

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.660
Is this because of the factor?

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:34.140
Sensei?

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:37.380
Boss?

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:38.570
Arima-<i>kun</i>?

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.930
It's time for you all to go home.

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.990
Thank you for having us.

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.190
Come back any time.

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:59.190
I'll say it again. I'm 
really sorry about Kodai.

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:03.610
Knowing him, he may
still be alive somewhere.

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:07.700
In a totally different place, perhaps.

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:10.580
Those are the same eyes.

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:14.870
Kodai would sometimes look
at me with just those eyes.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:20.380
Looking at that tapestry for
so long made my blood run cold.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.770
Me too.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:26.090
What did you talk to
Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i> about, boss?

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.970
Immortality.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:31.350
He's still young, though.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:32.330
Right?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:38.760
Did you consider the words
I spoke to you before?

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.770
The thing about swallows and sparrows?

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:45.820
Oh, you haven't yet?

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:54.360
Have you not noticed the thing
that exists within this mansion?

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:58.280
I can hear it...

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:02.880
The breath of 400 years...

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:41.570
"Episode 8: The Swallows
and Sparrows Know Not"

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:39.010
Episode 8: "The Swallows
and Sparrows Know Not."
